# MVI Presentation (Core)

UI layer uses **Model-View-Intent (MVI)**.

## File Naming

Each screen: `[FeatureName]Screen.kt`, `[FeatureName]ViewModel.kt`, `[FeatureName]Contract.kt`

## Contract.kt

```kotlin
// LoginContract.kt — single file for all three
data class LoginState(val username: String = "", val isLoading: Boolean = false)

sealed class LoginIntent {
    data class UsernameChanged(val value: String) : LoginIntent()
    data object Submit : LoginIntent()
}

sealed class LoginEffect {
    data object NavigateToHome : LoginEffect()
    data class ShowError(val message: String) : LoginEffect()
}
```

| Type | Role | Flow |
|------|------|------|
| `State` | Current UI snapshot | `StateFlow` |
| `Intent` | User actions | ViewModel `onIntent()` |
| `Effect` | One-shot events (nav, toast, snackbar) | `SharedFlow` / `Channel` |

## ViewModel Flow

1. Receive `Intent` → 2. Call UseCase → 3. Update `State` → 4. Emit `Effect` if needed

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — navigation flag in State
data class LoginState(val navigateHome: Boolean = false)

// ✅ GOOD
setEffect(LoginEffect.NavigateToHome)
```
